Unlike Decision Trees or Logistic Regression, the fitting process does **not** estimate coefficients or construct decision rules.

Instead, the algorithm simply stores the training observations in memory.

Whenever predictions are requested, the stored observations are searched to identify the nearest neighbors.

Predictions are obtained using the `predict()` method.

::: {#predict-knn .cell execution_count=8}
``` {.python .cell-code}
y_knn_pred = knn_clf.predict(X_knn_test)

print("Predicted labels:")
print(y_knn_pred)
```

